      "writtenOn": "2023-08-07T10:36:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand. This probably should never happen - I would guess VS will make sure it doesn\u0027t? And only VS will be able to connect?\nSo the attack should be blocked anyway.\nBut my question stands - if we do get an unexpected request, should we reject it, rather than ignoring it? (While leaving the existing connection up.)",
